只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH 结合 Kimi WebBridge","id":"gh:1328795096","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-webbridge","slug":"bill9109/dsh-webbridge","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH 结合 Kimi WebBridge"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-webbridge — Model tools that drive your REAL browser via Kimi WebBridge"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Install:** `dsh plugin --profile web add github:omdsh-dev/dsh-webbridge`"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**A DeepSeek Harness host plugin: it bridges Kimi WebBridge's local daemon into eleven `webbridge_*`"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" model tools, so the model operates **your own browser** — logins, cookies, and already-open tabs in"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"cluded — instead of a headless one.**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why this exists"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"When a model task has to touch a real website — a page behind your login, carrying your session and "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"your already-open tabs — a headless browser cannot help: it holds none of your state and would ask y"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"ou to authenticate all over again. `dsh-webbridge` exists to hand the model control of **your real b"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"rowser** while keeping that browser state strictly on your machine, never inside a model request."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"It ships **no browser-driving code of its own**: the actual work is done by the Kimi WebBridge daemo"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"n and browser extension. This plugin only translates that capability into model-facing tools on the "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"wser extension. This plugin only translates that capability into model-facing tools on the DSH side."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- **Real browser, not headless**: logins, cookies, and live sessions preserved\n- **Eleven model tool"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"s**: navigate / find_tab / snapshot / click / fill /\nevaluate / screenshot / list_tabs / network / c"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"lose_tab / close_session\n- **One task = one tab group**: a `session` name groups tabs, keeping tasks"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"\ncleanly isolated\n- **Local-first**: the daemon runs on your machine; browser state never leaves it\n"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"- **No KV-cache burden**: browser state lives outside the model request"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### Prerequisites (required!)"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"This plugin is an adapter — **without the pieces below, browser control does\nnot work**. You must in"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"stall Kimi WebBridge separately (an independent product\nby Moonshot AI; this plugin contains none of"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" its code). Full install and\nbrowser-extension setup instructions live on Kimi's official pages:\nfea"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"ture page /\nhelp center.\nIn short:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"If the daemon is not running, tools fail loud with a `daemon_unreachable`\nerror that tells you to ru"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"n `~/.kimi-webbridge/bin/kimi-webbridge start`."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Model experience"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Tool | Purpose |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| `webbridge_navigate` | Open a URL (new tab or current), set the tab group label |\n| `webbridge_fin"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"d_tab` | Re-select a tab this task opened, or borrow the user's active tab |\n| `webbridge_snapshot` "},{"id":"p18s3","text":"| Read the page's accessibility tree (text + `@e` refs) |\n| `webbridge_click` | Click an element by "},{"id":"p18s4","text":"`@e` ref or CSS selector |\n| `webbridge_fill` | Type into inputs / textareas / contenteditable edito"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"rs |\n| `webbridge_evaluate` | Run JS in the page (async supported) |\n| `webbridge_screenshot` | Capt"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"ure the page or one element to a file path |\n| `webbridge_list_tabs` | List the tabs opened in the s"},{"id":"p18s7","text":"ession |\n| `webbridge_network` | Inspect network activity (start/stop/list/detail) |\n| `webbridge_cl"},{"id":"p18s8","text":"ose_tab` | Close the current tab of the session |\n| `webbridge_close_session` | Close ALL tabs of th"},{"id":"p18s9","text":"e session (clears the tab group) |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### Session and closing rules (model contract)"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"These rules come from the upstream Kimi WebBridge skill and are part of the\nmodel contract:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- **One task = one session = one tab group.** Pick a `session` name at the\ntask's start and keep it "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"on EVERY call — never switch mid-task.\n- **Name it after the task**, not the site (`camping-research"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"`, not\n`kimi.com`).\n- **`group_title`** is the human-readable group label, set on the FIRST\n`navigat"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"e` of the task, written in the user's language.\n- **Closing is always user-initiated.** Call `webbri"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"dge_close_session` ONLY\nwhen the user explicitly asks to close/clear the tabs; never close tabs\nauto"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"matically at the end of a task."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Configuration"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"The daemon address defaults to `http://127.0.0.1:10086`. The plugin accepts\nno configuration today; "},{"id":"p23s2","text":"the `baseUrl` seam exists for tests."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The plugin is a DSH **bundle** (`package.json` declares `dsh.bundle`, and\n`cordis.patch.yml` carries"},{"id":"p25s2","text":" the patch). Install it into the `web` profile\nwith the standard `dsh plugin` mechanism — **no DSH s"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"ource changes and no\nhand-written patch**:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"For a stable install, pin the version:\n`dsh plugin --profile web add github:omdsh-dev/dsh-webbridge#"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"able install, pin the version:\n`dsh plugin --profile web add github:omdsh-dev/dsh-webbridge#v0.0.3`."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Internally the command runs `pnpm add <spec>` in the profile directory and\nautomatically appends pac"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"kages that declare `dsh.bundle` to\n`dsh.profile.bundles`. You can also clone it and install from a l"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"ocal path\n(for development):"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"The repository ships its build output (`lib/`), so the plugin works right\nafter installing — no buil"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"d step needed. After installing, **restart the Web\nUI** (production mode has no hot reload) and refr"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"esh the page — the\n`webbridge_*` tools become available to the model."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"### Upgrade"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"For a local-path installation, run `add` again against the replacement\ncheckout, then restart the We"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"installation, run `add` again against the replacement\ncheckout, then restart the Web UI and refresh."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"### Uninstall"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"The command runs `pnpm remove <pkg>` in the profile directory and removes\nthe package from `dsh.prof"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"ile.bundles`. After uninstalling, restart web and\nrefresh — the DSH built-in plugin (same row id `we"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"bbridge`) takes over again."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"### How it works"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Every tool call is one HTTP round-trip to the local daemon. The returned\npayload is folded into a co"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"mpact one-line `summary` plus the raw `detail`."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"### Known limitations"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"- **`event.isTrusted`** — sites that strictly check trusted input (some banking\nportals, captchas) i"},{"id":"p41s2","text":"gnore synthetic `click`/`fill`; the daemon's `cdp`\nescape hatch is not exposed as a tool yet\n- **Cro"},{"id":"p41s3","text":"ss-origin iframes** — snapshot/click/fill/evaluate operate on the top\nframe only\n- **Screenshots** —"},{"id":"p41s4","text":" the daemon writes to a temp path and returns the path; the\nmodel must use a Read tool to view the i"},{"id":"p41s5","text":"mage\n- **Daemon lifecycle** — tab groups are maintained by the daemon; restarting\nthe daemon clears "},{"id":"p41s6","text":"\n- **Daemon lifecycle** — tab groups are maintained by the daemon; restarting\nthe daemon clears them"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
